Article 2 (Methods of Exchange)
International money orders shall be exchanged by the following methods:
1. Card money order: An international money order certificate is issued in the remitting country and sent to the paying country, where the payee receives the relevant amount on the basis of the certificate;
2. List money order: A list of international money orders is prepared in the remitting country and sent to the paying country, where an international money order certificate is issued to the payee according to the list and the payee receives the relevant amount on the basis of the certificate;
3. Deposit money order: A list of international money orders is prepared in the remitting country and sent to the paying country, where the relevant amount is deposited into the payee's account according to the list.
